          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "The Moon appears to go through phases because it orbits Earth while reflecting sunlight, so only half of it is ever lit at once. From our viewpoint on Earth, the angle between the Sun, Moon, and our planet constantly shifts as the Moon moves along its path, revealing changing portions of that illuminated half. When the Moon lies between Earth and the Sun its dark side faces us, producing a new moon, whereas the opposite alignment shows the fully lit side as a full moon; the cycle repeats roughly every month.",
