          "reasoning": "I need to explain why the Moon appears to go through phases.\n\nThe Moon reflects sunlight rather than producing its own light. As it orbits Earth, the angle of sunlight hitting its surface changes. This creates the different phases we see.\n\nThe Moon's position relative to the Sun determines which side is visible from Earth. When it sits between Earth and the Sun, its dark side faces us as a new moon. When it is on the opposite side, we see the fully lit side as a full moon.",
